From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:45:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: add BCM4398 PCIe support

Add the BCM4398's PCIe id. On the Pixel 8 Pro (firmware 24.100.671.86.2
from the device's factory image) it joins WPA2, passes 50 to 87 Mbit/s
down and 47 to 70 Mbit/s up on 2.4 GHz, stays up across idle and deep
sleep, and survives driver reloads.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 3f5ea978c..969410ee3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -3629,6 +3629,7 @@ static const struct pci_device_id brcmf_pcie_devid_table[] = {
 	BRCMF_PCIE_DEVICE(BRCM_PCIE_4387_DEVICE_ID, WCC_SEED),
 	BRCMF_PCIE_DEVICE(BRCM_PCIE_4389_DEVICE_ID, WCC_SEED),
 	BRCMF_PCIE_DEVICE(BRCM_PCIE_4383_DEVICE_ID, WCC_SEED),
+	BRCMF_PCIE_DEVICE(BRCM_PCIE_4398_DEVICE_ID, WCC_SEED),
 	BRCMF_PCIE_DEVICE(BRCM_PCIE_43752_DEVICE_ID, WCC_SEED),
 	BRCMF_PCIE_DEVICE(CY_PCIE_54591_DEVICE_ID, CYW),
 	{ /* end: all zeroes */ }
